{"id": "unknown-2026-08-30-008", "date": "2026-08-30", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Sun"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Supply driven trucking market cycle explained in the data", "content": "<p>Tender volumes have gone nowhere for two years. Rejections have tripled. The data says this cycle has been defined by capacity leaving the market — not by surging freight demand.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.freightwaves.com/news/supply-driven-trucking-market-cycle-explained-in-the-data\">Supply driven trucking market cycle explained in the data</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.freightwaves.com\">FreightWaves</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "freightwaves", "url": "https://www.freightwaves.com/news/supply-driven-trucking-market-cycle-explained-in-the-data", "type": "rss"}]}
